{
  "_comment": [
    "SonicWall NetExtender SSL VPN provider.",
    "",
    "NetExtender is interactive (prompts for server / username /",
    "password) so this sample uses a tiny wrapper at",
    "`$HOME/.local/bin/netextender-connect` that the user writes",
    "with their pre-filled credentials. Example wrapper:",
    "",
    "  #!/bin/bash",
    "  exec netExtender --auto-reconnect --auto-dns \\",
    "      -u \"$USER\" -p \"$(secret-tool lookup app netextender)\" \\",
    "      -d MYDOMAIN vpn.example.com",
    "",
    "Pair with `secret-tool store --label='NetExtender'",
    "app netextender` to seed the password into the keyring.",
    "",
    "Status detection is process-based — `pgrep netExtender` returns",
    "0 only while the tunnel is up. statusLabelCmd extracts the",
    "tunnel IP from `ip -4 addr show ppp0` (NetExtender uses ppp0)."
  ],
  "id":               "netextender",
  "name":             "Work VPN (NetExtender)",
  "icon":             "󰦝",
  "statusCmd":        ["pgrep", "-x", "netExtender"],
  "statusOnPattern":  "^[0-9]+$",
  "statusLabelCmd":   ["sh", "-lc", "ip -o -4 addr show ppp0 2>/dev/null | awk '{print $4}' | cut -d/ -f1"],
  "connectCmd":       ["sh", "-lc", "$HOME/.local/bin/netextender-connect &"],
  "disconnectCmd":    ["pkill", "-x", "netExtender"],
  "pollSeconds":      5
}
